  "key_design_notes": [
    "Config is the central store: holds raw config arrays, ConfigSourceInterface references, and env-override logic.",
    "Config::get('policy') returns raw bool|array; PolicyConfig::fromConfig(Config) parses it into typed objects.",
    "Config::merge() has special deep-merge logic for 'policy' key: true→[] canonicalisation, per-list merge with deepMergeKeys=['ignore','ignore-id','ignore-severity','ignore-source'].",
    "JsonConfigSource uses JsonManipulator for targeted JSON edits; 'policy.*' keys use nested path traversal.",
    "ListPolicyConfig is abstract with AUDIT_* and BLOCK_SCOPE_* constants; subclasses are readonly value objects.",
    "AuditConfig is a separate lightweight class in Advisory namespace (not Policy); it only carries audit/format flags.",
    "PolicyConfig has immutable wither methods: withBlockingDisabled(), withIgnoreUnreachable(), withIgnoreSeverity(), withAudit().",
    "PolicyConfig::fromConfig() applies env-var overrides (COMPOSER_POLICY_ADVISORIES_BLOCK, COMPOSER_POLICY_MALWARE_BLOCK, COMPOSER_POLICY_ABANDONED_BLOCK, COMPOSER_AUDIT_ABANDONED) after parsing raw config.",
    "MalwarePolicyConfig overrides supportsInstallBlockScope()→true, making it block at install time.",
    "IgnorePackageRule, IgnoreIdRule, IgnoreSeverityRule are value objects stored in the policy list configs."
  ],

